    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "BODY",
      "narration_text": "First, metrics. Scores like BLEU and ROUGE count the words an answer shares with a reference answer. Here's a real calculation. The wrong answer, one hundred degrees, scores zero point eight seven. A correct answer in different words scores zero point two five. The score measured overlap, not truth. The survey notes these metrics often track human judgment poorly.",
